WEBVTT

00:08.550 --> 00:11.390
It seems these eyes
have failed me at last.

00:11.890 --> 00:16.640
But there's still something
I must see before I die.

00:19.520 --> 00:22.270
Your recent treatise impressed me.

00:22.770 --> 00:25.190
Professor! I'm honored.

00:27.490 --> 00:30.360
It's been 20 years
since your arrival here.

00:30.860 --> 00:32.780
Perhaps it's time.

00:35.540 --> 00:39.460
I shall hand over my universe to you.

00:46.920 --> 00:48.090
This is…

00:51.180 --> 00:52.760
This is my archival vault.

00:53.260 --> 00:54.890
Only I can enter.

00:55.930 --> 00:57.720
It's incredible.

00:58.220 --> 00:59.480
Take a look at this.

01:04.150 --> 01:08.190
This is the model of the universe
that I have devised and refined.

01:08.690 --> 01:11.450
Double epicycles. Amazing.

01:11.950 --> 01:15.700
The accuracy is faultless,
and the circular motions are uniform too.

01:16.200 --> 01:17.200
Yes.

01:17.290 --> 01:19.870
In all of human history,

01:20.460 --> 01:24.460
no one but me has achieved
this level of precision.

01:24.960 --> 01:28.340
This is the universe in its proper form.

01:32.090 --> 01:36.390
I have sacrificed all other possibilities,
options, and opportunities,

01:36.890 --> 01:40.730
and devoted my entire life
to refining this model.

01:41.730 --> 01:43.350
I never needed collaborators.

01:43.850 --> 01:47.940
I was certain that God would choose
only one person to reach the truth,

01:48.610 --> 01:52.240
and I swore I wouldn't tell anyone
until it was completed.

01:52.740 --> 01:55.160
Then why tell me?

01:55.240 --> 01:57.370
Because that one person

01:57.450 --> 02:00.160
may be you, not me.

02:01.870 --> 02:04.330
When you do research as long as I have,

02:04.420 --> 02:05.920
many things become clear.

02:06.420 --> 02:10.380
In terms of observations, theories,
calculations, and imagination,

02:10.880 --> 02:14.260
you are now superior to me in every way.

02:14.760 --> 02:17.510
The road to truth is perilously narrow.

02:18.010 --> 02:21.270
But you may be capable
of reaching the end.

02:21.770 --> 02:23.980
I could never…

02:25.270 --> 02:28.480
Perfecting the cosmos is beyond me.

02:30.070 --> 02:32.570
I won't ask you to start right away.

02:33.070 --> 02:35.660
If you're ever interested, just tell me.

02:45.210 --> 02:47.420
<i>Two epicycles…</i>

02:47.920 --> 02:50.460
<i>The universe in its proper form?</i>

02:50.960 --> 02:54.510
<i>Can I really… inherit such a task?</i>

02:55.470 --> 02:57.050
<i>What am I afraid of?</i>

02:57.640 --> 02:59.890
<i>Isn't audacity important?</i>

02:59.970 --> 03:03.180
<i>That's right! I have to be courageous!</i>

03:03.270 --> 03:04.890
<i>I will perfect the Professor's--</i>

03:08.060 --> 03:10.060
<i>What… was that?</i>

03:12.980 --> 03:15.320
My eyes are playing tricks on me.

03:15.400 --> 03:17.240
I must be exhausted.

03:20.870 --> 03:23.580
Don't worry.
It wasn't really the final phase.

03:26.160 --> 03:28.540
Professor, do you have a moment?

03:29.130 --> 03:31.290
It's about the completion of your model.

03:31.380 --> 03:34.170
Oh, have you given it some thought?

03:34.260 --> 03:37.930
Yes. Your ideas are brilliant.

03:38.430 --> 03:41.010
More than that, they will change history.

03:41.510 --> 03:42.680
However,

03:43.430 --> 03:45.810
I don't think I'm up to the task.

03:46.310 --> 03:49.190
I cannot carry the burden
of completing the cosmos.

03:54.190 --> 03:55.150
Is that so?

03:57.530 --> 04:00.200
Find me if you change your mind.

04:01.070 --> 04:04.700
But it'll be too late
when I'm on the verge of finishing!

04:11.580 --> 04:12.420
Professor.

04:13.630 --> 04:15.800
I know my own body.

04:16.300 --> 04:17.970
I don't have long.

04:18.550 --> 04:21.430
I've known it all this time,

04:22.430 --> 04:27.100
but I've never had the courage to ask you.

04:28.140 --> 04:29.140
Five years ago,

04:29.640 --> 04:31.900
when you turned me down,

04:32.400 --> 04:35.980
was it because you doubted my theory?

04:36.070 --> 04:38.990
Absolutely not!
Your theory is magnificent!

04:39.070 --> 04:42.030
I've never seen such an accurate model!

04:43.200 --> 04:44.870
Indeed.

04:44.950 --> 04:46.700
It is beautiful.

04:47.330 --> 04:49.870
It's precise, sublime,

04:49.960 --> 04:53.460
and in accordance
with Aristotle and the Holy Scripture.

04:54.210 --> 04:57.710
I've never once doubted that.

04:58.970 --> 05:01.590
But…

05:02.970 --> 05:04.890
It's never complete!

05:04.970 --> 05:07.350
No matter how much work I put into it!

05:09.100 --> 05:11.520
With my abilities,

05:11.600 --> 05:14.810
there will always be errors
that can't be overlooked.

05:15.320 --> 05:20.110
Even after a lifetime of work,
I could never reach my goal.

05:20.610 --> 05:23.070
No, I wish it was only that.

05:23.570 --> 05:25.620
What terrifies me the most

05:26.120 --> 05:28.040
is that my hypothesis

05:28.120 --> 05:31.620
may be completely wrong,
right down to its basic assumptions.

05:32.120 --> 05:34.830
If that's the case,

05:34.920 --> 05:38.800
what a waste I've made of my life!

05:38.880 --> 05:40.050
No.

05:40.630 --> 05:42.050
That can't be it.

05:42.550 --> 05:44.590
You couldn't complete your model

05:44.680 --> 05:47.510
simply because you lacked
the ability to do so.

05:48.010 --> 05:50.770
But that doesn't mean
your research was wrong!

05:50.850 --> 05:54.060
The life you dedicated to it
was not a mistake!

05:57.690 --> 05:59.030
One day…

05:59.860 --> 06:03.490
One day, tell me when we meet in heaven.

06:05.620 --> 06:06.910
<i>The truth.</i>

06:24.050 --> 06:26.050
Um, is the Professor--

06:26.140 --> 06:27.100
He's gone.

06:28.050 --> 06:29.390
I leave the rest to you.

06:29.470 --> 06:31.180
I'll be in the laboratory.

06:31.680 --> 06:33.180
Huh?

06:33.270 --> 06:34.810
Doing what?

06:36.150 --> 06:38.770
<i>Perfecting the cosmos.</i>

07:03.210 --> 07:05.720
ORB: ON THE MOVEMENTS OF THE EARTH

08:11.870 --> 08:14.120
Since we last met,
I have been generous enough

08:14.200 --> 08:17.330
to consider your ridiculous theory.

08:18.250 --> 08:21.880
And I've decided
to let you view my records.

08:22.460 --> 08:23.880
Really?

08:23.960 --> 08:26.130
However, I have one condition.

08:28.090 --> 08:31.220
You must prove true
what I know to be false.

08:31.720 --> 08:33.760
What exactly do you mean?

08:33.850 --> 08:35.470
Long ago,

08:35.560 --> 08:37.560
I saw something.

08:37.640 --> 08:40.020
No, I mistakenly saw something.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.520
Of course, such an error

08:42.610 --> 08:45.360
no longer concerns me now.

08:45.860 --> 08:49.490
<i>But it's true</i>
<i>that this one-time mistaken sighting</i>

08:49.570 --> 08:53.870
<i>planted the seeds of doubt</i>
<i>in my life's work.</i>

08:54.370 --> 08:57.370
That's why I want to take this opportunity

08:57.450 --> 09:00.410
to make certain that I was wrong.

09:00.500 --> 09:02.500
What are you talking about?

09:02.580 --> 09:04.590
What is it that you saw?

09:06.340 --> 09:09.010
Venus in its final phase.

09:10.760 --> 09:11.680
What?

09:11.760 --> 09:13.300
B-But that's--

09:13.390 --> 09:16.560
Venus in its final phase?
What does that mean?

09:17.140 --> 09:19.810
Earth is the center
of the geocentric model,

09:19.890 --> 09:22.600
so of course Venus
revolves around Earth too.

09:22.690 --> 09:23.520
EARTH, VENUS, SUN

09:23.600 --> 09:24.900
<i>That means Venus</i>

09:24.980 --> 09:28.360
<i>can only be illuminated by the Sun</i>
<i>from certain directions,</i>

09:28.440 --> 09:31.070
<i>and its shape always appears incomplete.</i>

09:31.650 --> 09:33.950
To see Venus in its final phase,

09:34.530 --> 09:38.790
<i>it would have to be illuminated</i>
<i>after circling behind the Sun.</i>

09:39.450 --> 09:40.870
<i>If that's the case,</i>

09:40.960 --> 09:44.880
<i>it would be more natural to think</i>
<i>the planets revolve around the Sun.</i>

09:45.380 --> 09:46.500
<i>And that would mean</i>

09:47.170 --> 09:50.460
the current model which places
the Earth at the center

09:50.550 --> 09:51.760
would be ruled out.

09:53.050 --> 09:54.220
Correct.

09:54.300 --> 09:56.180
But the opposite is also true.

09:56.260 --> 09:59.720
If you can't observe Venus
approaching fullness,

09:59.810 --> 10:02.020
heliocentrism would be ruled out.

10:02.100 --> 10:05.650
If you imbeciles are correct
in your hypothesis,

10:05.730 --> 10:10.530
then today, when Venus is small
and far away, it should appear full.

10:11.190 --> 10:15.320
Tonight, we will settle
the matter once and for all.

10:15.990 --> 10:18.990
<i>But first, I will test your eyesight.</i>

10:21.000 --> 10:25.170
I've drawn a shape as small
as a human pupil on that board.

10:25.750 --> 10:28.630
You must tell me
if it is a square or a circle.

10:28.710 --> 10:33.260
Do that, and I'll accept that your vision
is as good as mine was back then.

10:33.760 --> 10:36.930
I could never see something
that small from so far away.

10:37.720 --> 10:39.010
It's audacious to even try.

10:40.260 --> 10:43.810
Now, can you see
if it's a square or a circle?

10:45.520 --> 10:46.690
-No.
-Huh?

10:47.360 --> 10:48.940
It's neither.

10:49.520 --> 10:53.190
The shape is a half-circle
with the right side missing.

10:56.820 --> 10:58.950
Well… I guess you'll do.

10:59.910 --> 11:02.200
I'm going back to my room.

11:02.290 --> 11:04.250
Call me when Venus appears.

11:14.800 --> 11:16.050
-Excuse me.
-Huh?

11:16.550 --> 11:17.930
If…

11:18.010 --> 11:21.100
If I don't see Venus in its final phase,

11:21.600 --> 11:24.180
that means Earth
is the center of the universe

11:24.680 --> 11:28.350
and the bottom of everything, right?

11:28.850 --> 11:30.820
I'm worried.

11:30.900 --> 11:33.030
Somehow, I still feel

11:33.110 --> 11:36.030
like that is probably true.

11:36.110 --> 11:38.820
Is that because
the world you've experienced

11:38.910 --> 11:41.530
is full of suffering?

11:43.160 --> 11:44.290
Yes.

11:44.370 --> 11:46.290
I know how you feel.

11:46.790 --> 11:50.420
I've never thought
there was salvation on Earth either.

11:51.000 --> 11:55.130
We've been taught that our duty
is to ascend from this corrupt realm

11:55.210 --> 11:58.050
and make it to heaven.

11:58.840 --> 12:01.930
Even so, it has always bothered me.

12:02.510 --> 12:03.560
Our world

12:03.640 --> 12:06.230
holds too much beauty
for such a lowly place.

12:07.020 --> 12:08.730
Ferocious nature,

12:08.810 --> 12:10.350
primitive animals,

12:10.440 --> 12:11.690
and sinful humans…

12:12.270 --> 12:15.030
Even the fruits of tragedy like those

12:15.110 --> 12:17.570
are all beautiful in their own way.

12:18.070 --> 12:20.070
There must be a reason for that.

12:21.280 --> 12:24.490
And it may be that the Earth moves.

12:25.160 --> 12:27.160
If the Earth and the sky are one,

12:27.660 --> 12:31.880
then no matter how corrupt our world is,
it will never be without light.

12:33.750 --> 12:34.920
It's time.

12:35.920 --> 12:38.170
Venus will only be visible
for three hours.

12:39.550 --> 12:41.340
-Badeni.
-Huh?

12:41.430 --> 12:43.430
I have a question.

12:43.510 --> 12:46.100
Even if I say Venus appears full,

12:46.600 --> 12:49.730
couldn't Count Piast refuse to believe it?

12:49.810 --> 12:51.230
Yes.

12:51.310 --> 12:53.060
But even if that happens,

12:53.150 --> 12:55.070
at least I will know the truth.

12:56.900 --> 12:58.320
Are you worried?

12:58.400 --> 13:01.070
Yes, of course.

13:01.660 --> 13:04.530
No matter what the result is,

13:05.030 --> 13:08.200
what I see today will shape the universe.

13:08.790 --> 13:10.410
How could I not feel burdened?

13:10.920 --> 13:14.840
To be honest, I don't understand much

13:15.340 --> 13:17.590
about the things you two say or do.

13:17.670 --> 13:20.930
It's even less clear
how this affects my faith.

13:21.010 --> 13:24.850
Or rather, I was merely
caught up in all of this.

13:24.930 --> 13:27.560
I never had any desire
to change the world.

13:27.640 --> 13:30.640
I only wanted to go to heaven.

13:30.730 --> 13:35.560
I have no idea why I'm here
or doing any of this.

13:36.150 --> 13:38.150
These past few days

13:38.230 --> 13:41.360
have been the most puzzling of my life.

13:41.950 --> 13:45.740
Despite all of that,
what I find hardest to understand…

13:48.080 --> 13:52.160
is the fact that right now,
I want to see Venus in its final phase.

13:55.710 --> 13:56.590
In that case,

13:57.090 --> 13:59.710
there is nothing more we can do for you.

13:59.800 --> 14:00.630
No.

14:01.220 --> 14:03.630
But if you don't mind,

14:05.970 --> 14:07.260
<i>please hope.</i>

14:27.490 --> 14:28.410
<i>See it.</i>

14:30.740 --> 14:31.750
<i>Look full.</i>

14:33.000 --> 14:34.250
<i>I must see it.</i>

14:35.500 --> 14:36.960
<i>It must look full.</i>

14:38.590 --> 14:39.550
<i>See it!</i>

14:44.260 --> 14:46.970
EARTH

14:52.770 --> 14:53.980
It looks full.

15:01.530 --> 15:02.780
How mysterious.

15:03.780 --> 15:06.240
It's the same sky I've always seen,

15:06.740 --> 15:09.530
but now it looks so different.

15:10.530 --> 15:12.040
-I'll bet.
-Huh?

15:12.540 --> 15:16.580
This is what it means…
to learn something, I think.

15:21.000 --> 15:23.050
ORB: ON THE MOVEMENTS OF THE EARTH

15:23.130 --> 15:24.050
<i>Orb.</i>

15:26.800 --> 15:28.800
And so, Count Piast,

15:28.890 --> 15:30.220
since Venus appears full--

15:30.890 --> 15:32.510
Are you okay?

15:35.390 --> 15:37.270
I won't accept it.

15:37.350 --> 15:38.400
It can't be.

15:38.900 --> 15:40.690
It's a lie you've concocted.

15:40.770 --> 15:42.650
You're trying to trick me.

15:42.730 --> 15:43.940
We wouldn't!

15:44.030 --> 15:46.070
No, when I think clearly,

15:46.570 --> 15:50.700
even if Venus really appears full,

15:50.780 --> 15:54.330
that is only proof
that Venus revolves around the Sun.

15:54.830 --> 15:57.750
It's not proof that the Earth moves.

15:58.250 --> 16:00.330
My model is still correct!

16:00.420 --> 16:02.590
Yes. You're right.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.840
You could think of it that way.

16:06.260 --> 16:09.340
But is the universe
born from such thinking

16:09.430 --> 16:11.390
the natural product of God

16:11.470 --> 16:13.640
or the product of human stubbornness?

16:14.140 --> 16:16.390
How would it look to you?

16:19.980 --> 16:23.610
Young imbeciles like yourselves
could never understand!

16:23.690 --> 16:27.360
My history, the history of humankind,

16:27.440 --> 16:33.120
and years of accumulated learning
should never be so easily denied!

16:33.830 --> 16:34.950
Then what if

16:35.450 --> 16:39.370
there was something powerful enough
to instantly deny such learning?

16:39.870 --> 16:42.630
Something greater
than individual needs or will.

16:42.710 --> 16:46.340
Something that acts mercilessly
and without prejudice.

16:46.840 --> 16:48.880
If such a thing existed,

16:48.970 --> 16:51.180
what do you think it would be called?

16:56.220 --> 16:57.600
I would call it…

16:58.600 --> 17:00.140
<i>One day…</i>

17:00.230 --> 17:04.020
<i>One day, tell me when we meet in heaven.</i>

17:06.190 --> 17:07.610
I would call it

17:08.440 --> 17:09.950
truth.

17:20.210 --> 17:22.330
Here is the key to the archival vault.

17:22.420 --> 17:24.210
Everything is stored in there.

17:26.210 --> 17:28.090
Thank you very much.

17:28.170 --> 17:29.970
We accept it.

17:37.100 --> 17:38.310
Excuse me…

17:45.230 --> 17:46.860
How many…

17:47.360 --> 17:49.320
Just how many years of life

17:49.400 --> 17:54.110
do you think this key represents?

17:57.990 --> 18:00.080
Two thousand years.

18:02.000 --> 18:07.540
If all those years
did not lead to an answer,

18:08.250 --> 18:12.170
perhaps the truth never needed us at all.

18:12.260 --> 18:15.550
However, even if we were wrong,

18:15.640 --> 18:20.770
what we have written
will have meaning to history.

18:21.270 --> 18:24.140
I pray for that to be true.

18:35.820 --> 18:37.200
How was it?

18:37.870 --> 18:39.120
Incredible.

18:39.620 --> 18:42.080
I can fully concentrate
on research with these.

18:42.660 --> 18:43.830
For now,

18:43.910 --> 18:46.750
please carry the documents
we need to the village, Oczy.

18:46.830 --> 18:47.670
What?

18:47.750 --> 18:51.840
We can't work here
if we don't belong to this organization.

18:51.920 --> 18:53.340
Oh, right.

18:53.420 --> 18:55.590
As for you, Jolenta…

18:55.680 --> 18:57.890
I'll leave the choice to you,

18:58.680 --> 19:01.970
but I'd prefer it
if your involvement ended here.

19:02.060 --> 19:03.680
I'd like to work alone.

19:04.980 --> 19:06.060
Very well.

19:06.560 --> 19:10.940
Besides, I don't think
I have much else to offer at this point.

19:11.440 --> 19:14.780
Still, you've already been a great help.

19:15.490 --> 19:18.370
I rarely say anything like this,

19:18.870 --> 19:21.030
but I'd like to repay you if I can.

19:22.330 --> 19:25.750
In that case, please perfect
the heliocentric model.

19:26.830 --> 19:29.000
Yes. I promise.

19:29.500 --> 19:30.840
One more thing.

19:30.920 --> 19:33.710
If we happen to be arrested in the future,

19:33.800 --> 19:35.300
pretend you know nothing.

19:36.090 --> 19:39.260
That will be best for you
and for heliocentrism.

19:41.010 --> 19:42.310
I'll be going then.

19:42.810 --> 19:44.810
Oczy, please handle the records.

19:45.640 --> 19:47.230
Uh, right.

19:50.860 --> 19:53.440
Well… Thank you very much.

19:53.530 --> 19:54.820
I'll be going too.

19:59.160 --> 20:00.240
Excuse me!

20:01.660 --> 20:04.830
-Can I ask you one thing?
-Yes?

20:05.330 --> 20:08.500
What does it feel like

20:08.580 --> 20:10.330
to be able to read?

20:12.340 --> 20:14.920
Oh, uh, I know it's obvious to all of you,

20:15.010 --> 20:18.430
but until recently, the only person
I knew who could read

20:18.930 --> 20:21.890
was my mentor in the guild.

20:23.010 --> 20:26.520
Do you promise not to tell anyone
what I am about to say?

20:26.600 --> 20:29.650
Huh? Uh, yes.

20:30.350 --> 20:32.310
As a disciple of the Church,

20:32.400 --> 20:35.780
I know I shouldn't
use these words lightly.

20:36.530 --> 20:40.360
But I can't think
of any other way to express it.

20:41.620 --> 20:44.620
Reading and writing… are like miracles.

20:46.370 --> 20:51.170
Of course, I don't mean they're the same
as the miracles performed by our savior!

20:52.040 --> 20:55.050
Still, reading and writing are amazing.

20:55.550 --> 20:58.670
Using letters, a person
can cross space and time.

20:59.170 --> 21:02.720
I might shed tears
reading the news of 200 years ago

21:02.800 --> 21:05.680
or laugh at rumors from 1,000 years ago.

21:06.180 --> 21:08.560
Isn't that unbelievable?

21:09.060 --> 21:11.350
Our lives are trapped, beyond our control,

21:11.440 --> 21:14.310
in this day and age.

21:14.820 --> 21:17.690
But when I read,

21:17.780 --> 21:21.530
the great figures from the past
engage me in conversation.

21:22.030 --> 21:24.950
At that moment, I can escape the present.

21:25.450 --> 21:28.250
Thoughts put into writing
remain after we are gone,

21:28.750 --> 21:31.710
and they might spur someone
into action far in the future.

21:32.830 --> 21:34.500
What else could you call that

21:35.500 --> 21:37.170
but a miracle?

21:38.590 --> 21:40.880
It's… that great?

21:40.970 --> 21:42.630
Yes. It is.

22:53.870 --> 22:59.460
Finally… I can finally tell you.

23:02.380 --> 23:04.880
The truth.

24:57.000 --> 25:00.960
Subtitle translation by: Brad Plumb
